// Ch5 B10 "Kahre: the binding and the second verse" (act1_ch05.md). Letterboxed. Opens on the Matron
// banking after the fight: the slag cools from orange to black, her bound core glows on behind it,
// steady; no motes rise from her (she is bound).
// A10: the Tender opens the chamber behind the anvil-stone; Asha goes in alone, by rite. Toma's name
// for her is rung once, because Ch3 rang it. A11 (a single held frame; A10 → A11 cuts on a short
// fade): Kahre is bound light, steady, never drifting, white sparks in his mane that never fall; the
// keepsake hammer is a dark shape. Don't show the full form. No look passes between Kahre and Kerrid
// (Kerrid is outside). A08, the wait: Kerrid at the sea-facing arch; his eyes go once to the lantern
// on Rhen's shoulder, and away (gesture slot; he worked eight low tides beside its twin at Corrow).
// A12: Asha comes out walking, smiling, a little scorched around the eyes; released light lifts off
// her in slow upward spirals, less than in Ch3. Watch (ADR 0017, the Ch3 row): no stumble or catch at
// the door, and no summon shown at the door. The second verse: four #sung #lamptongue lines over
// hush_second_verse (Audio sets the final text). On "mir" the plume flashes and the thunder comes;
// nothing comes up out of the ground (the rhyme with Ch3's Drownbell; Rhen's fear, remembered, lands
// as relief: the only joke here). Ysolde's warmth closes it.
// Sets ch05_kahre_bound (vowbound.json bound_flag: Kahre callable from here on) and
// ch05_second_verse_sung (sleeve band 2). Kahre has no voice in Act I.
title: ch05_kahre
location: ch05/ashcrown
---
@letterbox on
@camera A08
@anim matron bank
@sfx matron_bank
@vfx glimmer_bound at=matron_heart
@wait 4.0
Tender as "Tender Ruwen" [soft_smile]: She'll sleep now. She always does. #line:ch05_kahre_001
@camera A10
@anim tender open_chamber
Toma [neutral]: We will be here, Lady Cantor. #line:ch05_kahre_002
Asha [soft_smile]: Toma. #line:ch05_kahre_003
Toma [soft_smile]: ...Asha. #line:ch05_kahre_004
@mark asha chamber_in walk
@fade out 0.6
@camera A11
@vfx glimmer_bound at=kahre_heart
@fade in 0.6
@wait 2.5
@fade out 0.8
@camera A08
@fade in 0.8
@music silence fade=2.0
Rhen [smile]: All those years in there with a hammer. You'd think he'd run out of things to hit. #line:ch05_kahre_005
@anim kerrid look_at rhen
@wait 0.8
@anim kerrid look_at sea
@anim rhen grin
Rhen [smile]: You've got a look like you're pricing it. #line:ch05_kahre_006
@wait 1.0
Ysolde [neutral]: The roll says he repaired the hinges of every temple door he passed through. Unasked. #line:ch05_kahre_007
@anim toma laugh
Toma [laugh]: That sounds like a smith. #line:ch05_kahre_008
@camera A12
@mark asha chamber_door walk
@vfx glimmer_lift at=asha motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@wait 1.5
Rhen [neutral]: Well? #line:ch05_kahre_009
Asha [laugh]: He was impatient with me. #line:ch05_kahre_010
Asha [smile]: I liked him very much. #line:ch05_kahre_011
<<if $ch05_found_quench_charm>>
    @anim asha look_at rhen
    Asha [soft_smile]: He'd have wanted that back, I think. He said nothing about it. Keep it. #line:ch05_kahre_012
<<endif>>
Ysolde [neutral]: The first verse is sung toward home. The second is sung to the mountain that taught it. #line:ch05_kahre_013
@anim asha face_crown_sing
@music hush_second_verse fade=0.5
Asha [tender]: Ish karra, ish karra, #line:ch05_kahre_014 #sung #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue (the Hush's second verse): keep as written. Audio sets the final text."
Asha [tender]: vey hal ennu, #line:ch05_kahre_015 #sung #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue: keep as written."
Asha [tender]: re ish, re ish... #line:ch05_kahre_016 #sung #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue: keep as written."
Asha [tender]: ...mir. #line:ch05_kahre_017 #sung #lamptongue #notr #tn:"Lamptongue: keep as written. Every verse ends on mir."
@sfx plume_thunder
@wait 1.0
@anim rhen brace
Rhen [afraid]: Is something going to come up out of the ground again? #line:ch05_kahre_018
Toma [tender]: Not this time, I think. #line:ch05_kahre_019
@wait 1.5
<<set $ch05_kahre_bound = true>>
<<set $ch05_second_verse_sung = true>>
@anim ysolde walk_past asha
Ysolde [neutral]: Lift your chin when you sing. It is better for the breath. #line:ch05_kahre_020
Asha [smile]: Yes, Scholar. #line:ch05_kahre_021
@letterbox off
@fade out 1.5
===
